# local working files, not part of the product tree
.claude/
.plans/
# The whole artifacts/ tree is local agent working material (reports, prompts,
# worker evidence, diorama shots). Nothing under it is tracked; ignoring the
# root keeps `git status` clean without piecemeal subpath rules.
/artifacts/
# Plan documents and investigation evidence live at the repo root while they
# are being worked. They are notes, not product, and a `git add -A` during a
# sync swept a dozen of them into a merge commit before CI's formatter caught
# it. Ignored so that cannot happen again; `git add -f` still works when one
# of them is genuinely worth keeping.
/plan-*.md
/plan-*-prompts/
/Executables.md
# Agent briefs. Same reason, plus these name the fork's own relay and
# environment hostnames, and this repository is public.
/glm-*.md

# T3 Trade themed assets & backups
assets/themed-t3trade/
assets/original-backup/
assets/.asset-theme-state.json

# Local test directory
test/

# generated icon variant mirrors (not for git unless confirmed)
assets/themed-t3trade-v*/
